From e91d5733d9afe40014d2049a6ac0af04b3836e31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@ziepe.ca>
Date: Wed, 4 Oct 2023 09:08:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 180/960] iommu: Fix return code in
 iommu_group_alloc_default_domain()

commit b85b4f30846bb169c114e99ceee17cc119f02a4b upstream.

This function returns NULL on errors, not ERR_PTR.

Fixes: 1c68cbc64fe6 ("iommu: Add IOMMU_DOMAIN_PLATFORM")
Reported-by: Dan Carpenter <dan.carpenter@linaro.org>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/8fb75157-6c81-4a9c-9992-d73d49902fa8@moroto.mountain
Signed-off-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/0-v2-ee2bae9af0f2+96-iommu_ga_err_ptr_jgg@nvidia.com
Signed-off-by: Joerg Roedel <jroedel@suse.de>
Signed-off-by: Jason Zeng <jason.zeng@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Yihua Jin <jinyihua@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Li Wei <liwei818@huawei.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/iommu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/iommu.c
index c9e2534e005e..0d3fc87aba46 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/iommu.c
@@ -1798,7 +1798,7 @@ iommu_group_alloc_default_domain(struct iommu_group *group, int req_type)
 	 */
 	if (ops->default_domain) {
 		if (req_type)
-			return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
+			return NULL;
 		return ops->default_domain;
 	}
 
-- 
